{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01RRYKMYhvZByMd5ExXBu7xJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"No ACL style available. I'll use article class with formatting that mimics a conference paper. Let me write the full paper now.\n\nLet me structure the paper carefully:\n\n## Paper Structure\n\n### Abstract (~150 words)\n\n### 1. Introduction (1.5 pages)\n- P1: LLM-as-judge ubiquity + style bias as dominant bias\n- P2: Gap: Likert misses it, no per-axis confound decomposition\n- P3: Our approach: CSD pipeline + dual contribution\n- P4: Contributions list (4 items)\n\n\n- P5: Related work overview\n- P6: Experiments roadmap\n\nNow I'm mapping out the core technical sections. I'll present the Controlled Style Decomposition methodology with style manipulation and NLI gating, then the dual measurement protocol and GEE-based confound decomposition. The experiments section will showcase the main Likert blindspot finding across different judges, sensitivity analysis comparing seven evaluation methods, and ablations on granularity effects.\n\nThen I'm detailing the per-axis confound structure, consistency checks across three architectures with formality and verbosity variations, and cross-benchmark generalization. The robustness analysis covers ablations on the NLI gate, placebo controls with double rewrites, rewriter independence validation, scaled replication studies, and cross-axis gradient analysis. I'll wrap up with discussion and conclusion sections, plus a brief limitations paragraph covering three key points.\n\nNow I'm calculating the page budget—this comes to roughly 8 pages total. I should consolidate some tables and tighten the writing to fit properly, though for a dream paper it's acceptable to run slightly long since it's meant to be review-ready rather than submission-ready. Let me start writing the full LaTeX document using a two-column format similar to ACL papers.","signature":""}],"stop_